# Copy to `loci.env` and fill in. `loci.env` is gitignored and kept out of the
# Docker build context, so nothing here is ever baked into an image layer.
#
#   cp loci.env.example loci.env
#   docker compose up
#
# Or without compose:
#   docker run -p 7777:7777 -v loci-data:/data --env-file loci.env loci

# Any server speaking OpenAI's POST /v1/chat/completions — llama.cpp, vLLM,
# Ollama, LM Studio, a gateway — so loci can run on your own hardware.
# Unset, it falls back to .llm-endpoint, then to DeepSeek's.
# LOCI_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://your-box:8080/v1/chat/completions

# Refused out loud when missing: the agent answers "no LLM key".
# LOCI_LLM_API_KEY is preferred — a token for your own server should not have to
# be filed under a vendor you are not using, and outside a container neither
# should a file: .llm-key resolves before .deepseek-key. Full order —
# LOCI_LLM_API_KEY, DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, .llm-key, .deepseek-key — so existing
# setups keep working untouched. (Neither file reaches a container: both are in
# .dockerignore, which is why the key comes in through the environment here.)
LOCI_LLM_API_KEY=

# Fails QUIETLY when missing — it falls back to deepseek-v4-flash, which is
# very likely not the model your endpoint serves. Set it whenever you set the
# key. The name is historical: it names the model on WHICHEVER server above.
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro

# Optional. Without it, research still runs but with no web search behind it.
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# --- semantic recall (memory) ---
# Landing in phases: today these six resolve and nothing else — the retriever
# that consumes them comes next, so setting them does not yet change `recall`.
# All six are optional, and an EMPTY value counts as unset for every one of them:
# `LOCI_EMBED_ENDPOINT=` with nothing after it turns semantic recall off rather
# than aiming loci at an empty URL. With no embed endpoint, `recall` is exactly
# what it is today — keyword, entity, recency and strength.

# Any server speaking OpenAI's POST /v1/embeddings, so the embedder can be your
# own hardware. Absent: semantic recall is off and recall stays lexical.
# LOCI_EMBED_ENDPOINT=http://your-box:8080/v1/embeddings

# Fails QUIETLY when missing, like DEEPSEEK_MODEL: it falls back to
# embed-qwen3-0.6b, which is very likely not what your endpoint serves.
# LOCI_EMBED_MODEL=embed-qwen3-0.6b

# The embedder gets its own token because the obvious setup is a hosted chat
# model plus a LOCAL embedder — two operators, two credentials. Absent: falls
# back to LOCI_LLM_API_KEY, then to sending no Authorization header at all.
# LOCI_EMBED_API_KEY=

# Absent: rerank is skipped. Fusion still runs, and the result says it was not
# reranked instead of pretending it was.
# LOCI_RERANK_ENDPOINT=http://your-box:8080/v1/rerank

# Quiet in the same way as the embed model: absent, it falls back to rerank-bge-m3.
# LOCI_RERANK_MODEL=rerank-bge-m3

# Absent: falls back to LOCI_EMBED_API_KEY, then LOCI_LLM_API_KEY, then to no
# Authorization header — rerank is usually served by the same box as embed.
# LOCI_RERANK_API_KEY=

# Where the substrate lives INSIDE the container. compose mounts a named volume
# here; change it only if you also change the mount.
LOCI_DATA=/data

# Deliberately not set here. The container listens on 7777 and compose publishes
# 7777; setting PORT would move the listener without moving the mapping, leaving
# a container that looks healthy and answers nothing.
# PORT=7777
